<mxCell id="g738" value="The reset works exactly when t is a multiple of λ. Steps 1 and 2 always give that; step 3 does on the 3-cycle (t = 3) and misses on the 4-cycle (t = 2) and the 2-cycle (t = 1)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=12;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="340" width="820" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="g739" value="&lt;b&gt;Answer:&lt;/b&gt; Step 3 meets (9, 7, 1) but the reset misses on the 4- and 2-cycles and finds 8 on the 3-cycle. Steps 1 and 2 reset to 8, 5, 8. Detection stays O(n), O(1)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=13;align=left;spacingLeft=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="394" width="820" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
